Respond strongly to consecutive ASCII or fullwidth zeros, more strongly
for longer runs. A zero repeated with one intervening token responds
weakly, with separate strengths for decimal points, commas, spaces and
hyphens. A zero after five gets a small extra response (the ending 50).
